  "reference_protocol": "Separate complete statements go to both public file modes and the pinned reference shell. Compare output, return codes, normalized diagnostics, and persisted catalog/rowids/rows/integrity. No expected result, target column, dependency or failing feature is rewritten to force agreement.",
  "implementation": "Certified syntax retains STORED flags and original expressions. Catalog sources cache bound dependency programs; declaration-order passes postpone unmet dependencies and diagnose loops at write preparation, including empty writes. A source-level row callback calculates typed generated registers before the ordinary Core constraint/write paths, carries UPDATE dependency closures into CHECK/FK processing, and follows ordinary NOT NULL replacement then generated-column recheck order. Generated preparation applies ordinary affinity before UPSERT excluded registers are observed. Scalar evaluation accepts an explicit builtin callback so schema date/time restrictions follow actual lazy calls and actual arguments. The public executable still executes Core; no C SQLite implementation is linked.",
  "audit_correction": "Only the textual live-audit pattern changed after the full fresh SQL evaluation: its old foreignKeys-only gate became the actual foreignKeys-and-row-preparation condition. The correction has its own receipt, with unchanged runtime source and executable hashes. All original failing audit evidence is retained; unrelated SQL suites were not redundantly rerun.",
  "proof_scope": "Existing independent token/character certification checks retained generated syntax. Catalog cache and empty-program component contracts are registered. A Lean runtime regression checks dependency positions, chained calculations after encoded reopening, xinfo metadata and rejection of a forged storage flag and an empty cyclic write. Source-free Core row/command semantics and prior theorem claims remain; no general generated-SQL equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unittest and fresh-seed survey share named families and one generator. Their 16 remaining failures are not a global compatibility percentage.",
